From e24104e473d9aa5113835261178593829b7eb2e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Beretta <joshuaberetta@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:13:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(subsequences): run automatic qual on a local
 OpenAI-compatible LLM

NLP_BACKEND=local sends automatic qual to LOCAL_LLM_URL
(/v1/chat/completions, e.g. llama.cpp's llama-server) instead of AWS
Bedrock, for offline installs. The Bedrock path is unchanged and stays
the default. No Bedrock client is created in local mode, and there is no
fallback model: a local failure is reported as a failed result.

It is one more client next to Mantle and Runtime (`LocalClient`, model
`LocalLLM`), used for every source type: transcripts, typed answers and
images. Image requests are converted from the Responses API format to
chat completions, with the image first, so llama-server reuses its
encoding across the analysis questions on the same image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
