From 92fe39bdf17d17e542e22a023f974962c4ca5a59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Beretta <joshuaberetta@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:32:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(subsequences): translate with a local
 OpenAI-compatible LLM

With NLP_BACKEND=local, automatic translation uses LocalTranslationService
instead of Google: same process_data() interface and failure messages, with
a translation prompt sent to LOCAL_LLM_URL. It only runs in a Celery worker
(or with CELERY_TASK_ALWAYS_EAGER): from a request it returns in_progress,
and the existing poll task finishes it, so slow CPU-only boxes don't hit
uWSGI's harakiri. Worker calls use LOCAL_LLM_TASK_READ_TIMEOUT.

Qual's local path now shares the same client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
