From 8e1eda8a18e5a3abdb9ca0cfededfbe724594e91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Beretta <joshuaberetta@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:06:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(subsequences): import a submission's supplement from
 another server

POST /api/v2/assets/<uid>/data/<root_uuid>/supplement/import/ takes another
server's GET .../supplement/ response and stores its versions as they are, so
an automatic transcript nobody has accepted yet arrives still pending review
(the supplement PATCH would run the action again or store it as manual).

- Versions merged by _uuid: importing again changes nothing; for a version on
  both sides only review state moves (accepted/verified kept from either side,
  earliest date)
- Every question/action in the body must be enabled on the asset (400 lists
  the missing ones); each action's data checked with its own result schema
  (validate_submission_supplement() checks nothing below the question: its
  per-question schemas are dicts of action schemas, not schemas)
- Needs change_submissions, as the supplement PATCH; a GET is 405, which lets
  clients (kobo-transfer) tell servers with the route from those without

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
